{"id":"gloire","lemma":"gloire","pos":"noun","rank":1651,"glosses":["glory"],"ipa":"/ɡlwaʁ/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ef/Fr-gloire.ogg/Fr-gloire.ogg.mp3","gender":"f","forms":{"plural":"gloires"},"formAudio":{"gloires":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/LL-Q150_%28fra%29-Eihel-gloires.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"Il est avide de gloire.","en":"He is eager to become famous.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"is","l":"être"},{"g":"avid, eager, desirous"},{"g":"of / from"},null]},{"text":"Elle tire toujours gloire de sa formation universitaire.","en":"She always prides herself on her academic background.","words":[{"g":"she / it"},{"g":"to draw, drag, pull","l":"tirer"},{"g":"always"},null,{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"his"},{"g":"formation"},{"g":"university"}]},{"text":"À vaincre sans péril, on triomphe sans gloire.","en":"Nothing ventured, nothing gained.","words":[{"g":"to / at"},{"g":"to defeat, vanquish"},{"g":"without"},{"g":"peril, danger"},{"g":"we / one"},{"g":"triumph"},{"g":"without"},null]}]}